      "source": "tr_M(word) via sum_lambda y_lambda chi^lambda (exact-Fraction seminormal) vs Tr(K rho(word))/(1+q^2)^n (tensor picture), D/T/3He free and atom, as series in eps to every computed order and as exact rationals at q = 8/7. Both h-placements match — and must: each is an H_n(q)-trace with the Markov property and loop value z_D, and the Markov trace with a given loop value is unique (Jones/Ocneanu). The docstring's expectation that only one would pass was wrong; recorded, not hidden."
    },
    {
      "name": "R_matrix_expansion_gives_Y_diag_0_m1_p1_0_and_W_minus_E2121",
      "computed": "1",
      "expected": "1",
      "passed": true,
      "source": "q = 1 + eps exactly; h = q - 1/q = 2 eps + (-1) eps^2 + ... so on the diagonal (e11, e12, e21, e22) the eps-coefficient of R is (1, 0, 2, 1) = 1 + (0, -1, +1, 0) and the eps^2-coefficient is (0, 0, -1, 0). Hence Y = diag(0,-1,+1,0): sY = -Ys by inspection, and Tr(Y P) = 0 for any permutation P by the e12 <-> e21 count symmetry. These are the objects the c2 derivation uses."
    }
  ],
